      "beforeContent": "# ADR-012 — A release binds to the destination the clients poll, and proves the delivered artifact\n\nDate: 2026-10-22. Tickets T-981, T-982, T-983, T-984 (improve cycle imp-vacuum34-wintage-20261022-1, RUN-1/IMP-001, IMP-002, IMP-003, IMP-004).\n\n## Context\n\nThe distribution moved from `github.com/vacterro/Wintage` to\n`gitlab.com/vacuum34/wintage` in release 1.36.10, and the ledger recorded the\nGitHub side as dead: `E-4321` says `git ls-remote` answers `403 Your account is\nsuspended`, the raw URL answers `404`, and the repository page answers `404`.\nThat is false. `git ls-remote github` exits 0, the GitHub API reports the\nrepository as public, `archived: false`, pushed at `2026-10-21T04:14:25Z`, and\nthe operator's own repair `052f416` was committed on that side. Two live public\nremotes now serve two different versions of the same product, and the\ndifference is invisible to every gate in this repository, because every gate\nreads the working tree.\n\nTwo things went missing in that migration, and both are release safety, not\ndocumentation.\n\nFirst, the release never knew WHERE it pu
