    {
      "beforeContent": "# SAIPEN protocol incidents -- index\n\n**Start here.** This is the one entry point for defect reports written\nBY agents working in other projects ABOUT the SAIPEN protocol, guard and\nruntime. Before this file they landed in four unrelated roots, so the\nnext agent could only find the ones it already knew about.\n\n`SRC-053` declares this root and its `inbox/claimed/resolved/invalid/`\n`evidence/` lifecycle. It is REGISTERED AND NOT IMPLEMENTED: there is no\n`saipen defect emit`, and `saipen defects` answers `RUNTIME_DRIFT`. Every\npacket below was therefore hand-mirrored by its reporter. That is why this\nindex exists and why it is maintained by hand until the command lands.\n\nThis index **binds bodies, it does not move them.** Each entry carries an\nabsolute path and a sha256 of the bytes as of generation. A body that is\nedited or moved shows up as a digest mismatch instead of as a silent\nsecond copy -- one report living in two places is the exact drift the\none-root rule exists to stop.\n\n- generated: 2026-09-18 20:30 local; refreshed 2026-09-19 by T-1394 triage\n- freshness cutoff: eve
---
