{
  "createdAt": "2026-10-05T23:35:43.026Z",
  "files": [
    {
      "afterContent": "T-902: Reddit runs the lean CSS-only path\n\nReddit is a continuously mutating shreddit SPA: a feed scroll appends posts,\ncomments and media shells faster than a document-wide sweeper can settle, and\nusers reported renderer crashes while that machinery was running on reddit.com.\nSTATUS_ACCESS_VIOLATION is a Chromium native renderer fault, so this commit does\nnot claim to fix it or to be its root cause: it removes the expensive\ndocument-wide repaint work from Reddit and keeps the theming on the lean\nCSS-only path, which is the part a userscript can actually own.\n\nOne authoritative gate, no second Reddit-only mode: HIGH_CHURN_HOST gained one\nterm, IS_REDDIT, so every mechanism that already keyed off CSS_ONLY_MODE turns\noff on reddit.com at once -- no body-subtree repaint MutationObserver, no\ndocument-wide getComputedStyle sweeps, no CSSOM :hover surgery, no force passes,\nno per-shadow-root repaint observer, no timers. Shadow DOM theming is NOT\ndisabled: the attachShadow hook still injects the bounded creation-time\nstylesheet each shreddit-* component needs, and stops there.\n\nThe sur
---
