  "files": [
    {
      "beforeContent": "\"\"\"T-1951: a retired module must not be resurrected into every new install.\n\n`bootstrap/install_ownership.py:record()` merges the destination's state into a\nfreshly staged generation before the swap. Its documented contract is \"an\nupgrade preserves extra files\", but a file that sits INSIDE a manifest-declared\nruntime tree is not a user note: the runtime identity\n(`saipen_engine.runtime_surface.require_runtime_generation_identity`) hashes\nevery member of that tree, so one extra file there makes the installed\ngeneration permanently unequal to its source.\n\nThe consequence is not cosmetic. The scheduled injector compares the copy's\nidentity against the source's; a file the new generation no longer ships kept\nthe comparison false forever, so every publication rolled back, and the\nrollback left the PATH launcher and every installed hook `--saipen-root`\nnaming the generation the run had just rejected. That is the authenticated\ningress deadlock T-1951 was filed for.\n\nThe tests below are behaviour, not source text: they run `record()` on a real\ntwo-directory pair and then ask the q
---
