      "beforeContent": "// T-415: the native operator ingress of the ZAICODE host.\n//\n// A `cc` typed by the operator and a `cc` produced by the model are the same\n// bytes. SAIPEN does not take the word of whoever forwards them: the engine\n// digests the operator's own text (`ingress_digest`) and looks for a host\n// ingress envelope that carries the SAME digest AND a broker-sealed\n// `operator_origin`. A model can write a file, a transcript or an envelope --\n// it can produce a matching digest -- but it cannot produce a sealed origin,\n// because the broker mints one only for an event it proved came from the\n// registered host application.\n//\n// The ZAICODE side of that contract is three small things:\n//\n// 1. the CLASSIFICATION: only the CLI ingress may say `real_user`, so this\n//    module reads the already-classified provenance and never the raw wire;\n// 2. the ENVELOPE: the operator's verbatim bytes, digested exactly as SAIPEN\n//    digests them, bound to the delivering session;\n// 3. the DELIVERY: the installed SAIPEN ingress hook for this host, which\n//    asks the broker to seal the origin and 
