{
  "createdAt": "2026-10-23T16:17:08.179Z",
  "files": [
    {
      "beforeContent": "# The ZAICODE operator ingress (T-415)\n\nA `cc` typed by the operator and a `cc` produced by the model are the same\nbytes. SAIPEN does not take the word of whoever forwards them: the engine\ndigests the operator's own text and looks for a host ingress envelope that\ncarries the SAME digest AND a broker-sealed `operator_origin`. A model can\nwrite a file, a transcript or an envelope — it can produce a matching digest —\nbut it cannot produce a sealed origin, because the broker mints one only for an\nevent it proved came from the registered host application.\n\nThis file is the cross-repository contract: what the product does, what the\ninstalled SAIPEN host provides, and how the two are proven to fit.\n\n## What the product does (this repository)\n\n1. **Classification** — `zcode-protocol-v4/commands/input-intent.ts` is the only\n   place that may classify a submission as `real_user`; a wire-declared\n   `real_user` is demoted to `unknown`. `operator-ingress.ts` reads that\n   provenance and never the raw wire.\n2. **The carrier** — `continue-carrier.ts` writes the operator's verbatim bytes\n  
---
