      "beforeContent": "{\n  \"schema_version\": 1,\n  \"description\": \"Single declarative host adapter registry (SRC-028:R008). Every consumer -- tools/saipen_engine/admission.py, bootstrap/inject.ps1, bootstrap/inject.sh, tools/autoinject.py, status/freshness reporting and the parity tests -- reads host identity, install surfaces and enforcement capability from THIS file. No consumer may keep a second handwritten host inventory. declared_strength is what the adapter CLAIMS for an installed, current, healthy install; effective enforcement is computed at runtime by admission.effective_strength and is never stronger than the installed state proves. `response_enforcement` is a SEPARATE claim about the FINAL-RESPONSE contract only (EXEC-RESPONSE-01), never derived from `declared_strength`: MECHANICAL means a host hook can refuse the outgoing final message, ADVISORY means the contract reaches the model as instructions only, UNAVAILABLE means the host has no final-response surface at all. A host may claim MECHANICAL only with a `response_hook` token its own `hook_artifact` actually contains, and host-level trust evidence 
