FILE: C:\Users\vac34\.zcode\cli\artifacts\sess_dd5c3411-1c7a-4834-9765-9ad8b938b00d\call_00_391t5tul9pilhyads5o7r44f-tool-result-57f8772a-338b-4d9a-a4d3-19ac22f4819c.json
{
  "createdAt": "2026-10-06T01:46:26.677Z",
  "files": [
    {
      "beforeContent": "\"\"\"Guard-side client of the SAIPEN host-authority broker.\n\nThe Claude Code hook and the canonical engine never mint admission, and this\nmodule is where they stop pretending they can. It asks the broker, and the\nbroker answers after identifying the asking process from the operating system.\nNothing here decides an admission state: the verdict, the capability and the\nledger record all come back from the broker, and a request this module cannot\ndeliver is reported as unreachable rather than invented.\n\nRecovery is bounded and explicit. When no broker answers, the client attempts\nexactly one automatic start -- and only when its own process is a descendant of\na registered host application, because starting a service on behalf of a random\nsame-user shell is neither useful nor safe -- then retries the handshake once.\nEvery step is recorded in the returned `recovery` block so the diagnostic the\noperator sees can name the component that failed and the recovery that was\nattempted, instead of repeating that an authority \"is required\".\n\nThe degraded fallback is deliberately NOT automatic
---
FILE: C:\Users\vac34\.zcode\cli\artifacts\sess_dd5c3411-1c7a-4834-9765-9ad8b938b00d\call_00_93fo7odo7s51a5zpxva24fq7-tool-result-1efef7e3-5ef2-40a5-a321-830cab2a27fb.json
{
  "createdAt": "2026-10-06T01:50:16.747Z",
  "files": [
    {
      "beforeContent": "\"\"\"PROTOCOL-ADMISSION-01 acceptance: no current admission, no reply.\n\nEvidence classes, kept apart on purpose (a green in one says nothing about\nanother):\n\n* OWNER      -- `protocol_admission` states, fingerprints, invalidation.\n* LAYERING   -- `response_surface.gate_final_response`: admission, EXEC-RESPONSE\n                and chat style are separate layers and never compensate.\n* HOST       -- the Claude Code hook: bootstrap, pre-generation block, same-turn\n                init, runtime-authored diagnostics.\n* ORACLE     -- the pre-fix subject: the SAME `response check --classify` oracle\n                every host called before admission existed. The carriers that\n                escape it are the ones the repaired path must refuse.\n* DATA       -- the host capability matrix and the registry admission policy.\n\n`chat_style` false-positive rates and the style tests are NOT admission\nevidence and appear nowhere here.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport json\nimport os\nimport shutil\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nimport tempfile\nimport unittest\nfrom unitt
---
FILE: C:\Users\vac34\.zcode\cli\artifacts\sess_dd5c3411-1c7a-4834-9765-9ad8b938b00d\call_00_93r1p1usrkhmypo1y02m2i5q-tool-result-e801f88d-4360-4373-8ded-207967c0705a.json
{
  "createdAt": "2026-10-06T01:45:01.445Z",
  "files": [
    {
      "beforeContent": "\"\"\"PROTOCOL-ADMISSION-01: the one runtime owner of session protocol admission.\n\nDefect class: an assistant reply reaches the user although the protocol\nauthority that governs it was never established in that session. The failure\nwas reported from the field as a model that \"did not read STYLE.md\" and \"did not\ninvoke the voice skill\" and then wrote a paragraph explaining why it had not.\nPost-generation checks (EXEC-RESPONSE, chat style) measure a reply that already\nexists; they cannot decide whether the speaker was allowed to speak. That\ndecision is this module's alone.\n\nLayering, each layer answering a different question and none able to\ncompensate for an earlier failure (`response_surface.gate_final_response`):\n\n    binding          which project and host does this protocol apply to?\n    ADMISSION        was the required authority actually established?   <- here\n    EXEC-RESPONSE    is the operational response structurally valid?\n    chat style       does the visible reply obey language and style?\n\nAdmission is machine-derived, never asserted. The evidence is what the ru
---
