      "beforeContent": "# Changes against the BZ2 1.3 public DLL source\n\n## VRV 0.3.19: native multiplayer commands\n\n- **Classic destruction passage** (T-519, `ExplosionWave.h`,\n  `ClassicWrecks.cpp`): the installed `ordin_a.wav` accompanies actual\n  destruction as a delayed spatial passage, initially faster/higher then\n  slower/lower and fading as its packet moves away. It covers near deaths\n  too, preserves the pressure/rumble layers and scrap exclusion, and stops\n  active cues on reload. BZCC's copy is 44.1 kHz, so the runtime projection\n  plays a 22050 Hz copy made from it (`vrv_classic_pass.wav`), leaving the\n  rise room under `SetRate`'s 44100. See `EXPLOSION_WAVE.md`.\n\n- **Moving-source Doppler** (T-518, `ClassicAudioHost.h`,\n  `docs/CLASSIC_AUDIO.md`): restore the native spatial allocator when a pilot\n  profile's hidden 3D channel count or spatial master gain is zero. Approaching craft and ordnance\n  sound higher and faster, receding ones lower and slower, through the\n  engine's own Doppler calculation. Preparation enables the channels before\n  playable objects create sounds; existing positive
