      "afterContent": "# Test-to-child edge inventory (T-324)\n\nEvery SAITULS test entrypoint that could reach the operator's desktop, the\nchild it starts, and the capability that makes it safe or unsafe. The rule the\nwhole table enforces: an edge is admitted only when the capability it needs is\nadmitted by `tests/test_safety.py`. Being idle is not consent, an environment\nvariable alone is not isolation, and restoring the cursor, focus or clipboard\nafterwards does not make an intrusive action non-intrusive.\n\nCapabilities: `NON_INTRUSIVE` (default lane, always admitted),\n`ISOLATED_LIVE_INPUT`, `ISOLATED_LIVE_CLIPBOARD`, `ISOLATED_SHELL_MUTATION`.\nThe last three require a verified disposable guest: a JSON marker carrying\n`guest_id`, `disposable: true` and a `host_fingerprint` that differs from this\nmachine's. A missing, malformed or self-minted marker fails closed.\n\nAdmission points: `test_safety.require()` in Python, `test_safety.py admit\n<CAP>` shelled from PowerShell. Rejection codes: `DENIED` (module exit 1),\n`BLOCKED_ENVIRONMENT` (module exit 3, no usable guest evidence).\n\n## Python entrypoints\n\n
---
